these people have been queuing for hours  to refill an oxygen tank  that a relative suffering from covid19  depends on to survive  normally hospitals would supply oxygen  to patients but many have run out  so people are having to buy them from  private companies  each oxygen bottle costs 68 and supply  is outstripping demand and as people's  tempers rise  police have been deployed  we can't wait any longer there's no  service at the hospital  the health system in the brazilian state  of amazonas is on the verge of collapse  and a national vaccine rollout has yet  to begin  the air force has flown emergency  supplies of oxygen from sao paulo to the  city of manaus  and airlifted premature babies to other  states  from hospitals overwhelmed by a surge in  coronavirus infections  on friday people in cities across brazil  held protests and appealed for more help  from the government  brazilians are dying this is total  neglect it is unacceptable  we are dependent on neighboring  countries for oxygen it's an outrage  president jaya bolsonaro has repeatedly  played down the risks of covid19  and he's defending his handling of the  pandemic response  we're always doing what we have to do  the problem in manas is terrible but  we've done our part by providing  resources and means  today the armed forces have launched a  field hospital there  the health minister was there on monday  and provided oxygen  these health workers are celebrating  because some of their patients are being  transferred to hospitals in other states  that are better equipped for them but  not everyone is being airlifted to safer  environments  and the world health organization is  warning brazil's health system is  beginning to implode  victoria gatenbee al jazeera
 

